-- The catalog as shipped content, not a code-bundled fallback.
--
-- The app carried three copies of it: 25 recipes in the client bundle, 2 in a
-- server constant, and 2 in the database. The database is what real users are
-- served, so they saw 2 recipes while the other 23 sat unused in the JS bundle,
-- and the seeded rows had Cyrillic difficulty values that the "Easy/Medium/Hard"
-- filter could never match. This makes the database the single source of truth;
-- the bundled copies are deleted in the same change.

